    {
      "name": "Technical",
      "num_qs": 30,
      "marks": 50,
      "question": [
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290857",
          "text": "Which of the following is not part of the Ethernet frame?<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  Preamble<br /> </li><li>  CRC<br /> </li> <li> Source address<br /> </li>  <li> Type or Length  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290856",
          "text": "Which of the following algorithm always guarantees that the transmitted packet is forwarded using minimum number of hops?<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  Link state routing<br /> </li><li>  Distance vector routing<br /> </li> <li> Flooding<br /> </li>  <li> Load shedding  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290855",
          "text": "<p>Suppose a user turns on a computer, starts a browser, types http://www.thegatebook.in&nbsp;and hits ENTER. Which of the following protocols would probably NOT be used at any point to serve this request?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>HTTP</li>\n    <li>TCP</li>\n    <li>UDP</li>\n    <li>SMTP</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn,network-protocols",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290854",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following statements is TRUE about network devices?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>Ethernet switches will always send received frames out to all interfaces (except the one on which the packet was received).</li>\n    <li>Both IP routers and Ethernet hubs drop packets when there is congestion.</li>\n    <li>Ethernet switches learn the location of hosts on their network by observing the frames they process.</li>\n    <li>If an IP router doesn’t know the location of a destination IP address in a packet it receives, it will flood the packet out to all interfaces (except the one on which the packet was received).</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn,routers-bridge-hubs-switches",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290853",
          "text": "Which of the following field of the IP header may not be used by destination's IP layer while doing the defragmentation?<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  Offset<br /> </li><li>  Identification<br /> </li> <li> More Fragment bit<br /> </li>  <li> Do not fragment  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290852",
          "text": "Which of the following statements about datagrams sent by a node in a network using $IPv4$ protocol is (are) TRUE?<br />\n<br />\nI. Datagrams at the source must be the size of the smallest maximum transmission unit (MTU) of all the links on a path to the destination.<br />\nII. Datagrams may be fragmented during routing.<br />\nIII. Datagrams are reassembled only at the destination.<br />\n<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  II only<br /> </li><li>  III only<br /> </li> <li> I and III<br /> </li>  <li> II and III  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290851",
          "text": "Which utility would we use to test all $7$ OSI layers?<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  Ping<br /> </li><li>  Trace route<br /> </li> <li> Telnet<br /> </li>  <li> Show ARP  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290850",
          "text": "Raju sends Rani a TCP packet containing a $\\text{2 byte}$ payload with sequence number $100$. If Rani receives it, with which acknowledgement number does she reply?<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $99$<br /> </li><li>  $100$<br /> </li> <li> $101$<br /> </li>  <li> $102$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290849",
          "text": "Which of the following is a stateless protocol ?<br />\nI. IP<br />\nII. HTTP<br />\nIII. TCP<br />\nIV. BGP<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  Only I<br /> </li><li>  Only I and II<br /> </li> <li> Only II and IV<br /> </li>  <li> Only III and IV  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290848",
          "text": "A server transmits one frame of a video every second, and the client starts playing the video at one frame per second as soon as the first frame arrives. Suppose the first ten frames arrive at times $0, 1.2, 1.99, 4.17, 4.01, 5.03, 8.05, 7.50, 8.90, 8.99,$ all in seconds. How many frames reach the client too late for playout?<br />\n<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $7$<br /> </li><li>  $3$<br /> </li> <li> $6$<br /> </li>  <li> $5$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290847",
          "text": "Consider two links, $(A,B)$ and $(B,C)$, with propagation delays of $d1$ and $d2$, respectively. Assume that $\\text{host A}$ sends $\\text{M packets}$ to $\\text{host C}$ using a sliding window flow control protocol with a window of size $W$.<br />\nWhat is the minimum time it take to send all packets from $A$ to $C$ when the flow control protocol is implemented end-to-end between $A$ and $C$ ?<br />\nNote: Transmission delays are negligible<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $2(d1+d2) \\left \\lceil \\left ( \\dfrac{M}{W} \\right ) \\right  \\rceil$<br /> </li><li>  $(d1+d2) MW$<br /> </li> <li> $2(d1+d2)\\left \\lceil \\left ( \\dfrac{W}{M} \\right ) \\right  \\rceil$<br /> </li>  <li> $2(d1+d2)W$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290846",
          "text": "Consider a link $(A,B)$ with bandwidth $\\text{1 Kbps}$ and propagation delay $\\text{300 msec}$ and stop and wait protocol is used from $A$ to $B$ and Acknowledgements are piggybacked. Frame size is same for $A$ and $B$ and it is $\\text{100 bits}$. Assume that $B$ always have the data to send to $A$.<br />\n<br />\nThe Throughput for $A$ in this model is ___________ $ \\text{Kbits/sec}$?<br />\n<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $200$<br /> </li><li>  $250$<br /> </li> <li> $333$<br /> </li>  <li> $125$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290845",
          "text": "TCP is sending data at $\\text{1 megabyte per second}$. If the sequence number starts with $92000$, how long does it take before the sequence number goes back to zero?<br />\n<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $7295.12$<br /> </li><li>  $6295.87$<br /> </li> <li> $7592.86$<br /> </li>  <li> $4294.87$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290844",
          "text": "A computer on a $6-Mbps$ network is regulated by a token bucket. The token bucket is filled at a rate of $\\text{1 Mbps}$. It is initially filled to capacity with $\\text{8 megabits}$.<br />\nIf the system is initially idle for $\\text{2 sec}$ then how long can the computer transmit at the full $\\text{6 Mbps}$ speed?<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $\\text{1.6 sec}$<br /> </li><li>  $\\text{2.6 sec}$<br /> </li> <li> $\\text{3.6 sec}$<br /> </li>  <li> $\\text{4 sec}$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290843",
          "text": "<img alt=\"GATEBOOK-2019 Grand Test CN-15\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"/> <br />\nFor the above network, which constraints on $x$ and $y$ guarantee traffic from $B$ to $C$ will always flow through node $A$?<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>   $x &gt; 4$<br /> </li><li>   $y + x &lt; 6$<br /> </li> <li>  $y + x &lt; 4$<br /> </li>  <li>  $x &lt; 4$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290842",
          "text": "<p>In a communication link out of $\\text{p packets}$ one packet will be lost. If stop and wait protocol is used then expected number of retransmissions for a packet?<br>\n&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$\\dfrac{p}{p-1}$</li>\n    <li>$p$</li>\n    <li>$\\dfrac{1}{p-1}$</li>\n    <li>$\\dfrac{1}{p}$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn,probability",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290841",
          "text": "<p>An organization has a class $C$ network and wants to form subnets for four departments, with hosts as follows.<br>\n$$\\begin{array}{|c|c|}&nbsp; \\hline Department &amp; \\text{No. of hosts required} \\\\ \\hline W &amp; 72 \\\\ \\hline X &amp; 35 \\\\ \\hline Y &amp; 20 \\\\ \\hline Z &amp; 18 \\\\ \\hline &nbsp; \\end{array}$$<br>\nWhat is the possible subnet masks for the departments $W,X,Y\\:&nbsp; and \\: Z$<br>\n&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$W:255.255.255.223, \\: X:255.255.255.192,\\: Y\\&amp;Z :255.255.255.128$</li>\n    <li>$W: 255.255.255.128,\\: X :255.255.255.192,\\: Y\\&amp;Z : 255.255.255.224$</li>\n    <li>$W: 255.255.255.192,\\: X :255.255.255.128,\\: Y\\&amp;Z : 255.255.255.224$</li>\n    <li>$W: 255.255.255.223,\\: X \\&amp; Y\\&amp; Z : 255.255.255.223$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn,subnetting,ip-addressing",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290840",
          "text": "A network on the internet has a subnet mask $255.255.240.0$. the maximum no of hosts it can have is<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $1022$<br /> </li><li>  $4094$<br /> </li> <li> $2046$<br /> </li>  <li> We can not determine  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290839",
          "text": "<p>Assume all frames have size $\\text{F bits}$, and the propagation delay on the link is $\\text{P sec}$, and the bandwidth is $\\text{B bps}$. Assume also that the receiver piggybacks acknowledgements on frames going to the sender.<br>\nWhat should be the minimum window size $n$ (in frames)&nbsp;at the sender in order to effectively use the bandwidth?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$2+\\dfrac{2PB}{F}$</li>\n    <li>$1+\\dfrac{2PB}{F}$</li>\n    <li>$\\dfrac{2PB}{F}$</li>\n    <li>$1+\\dfrac{PB}{F}$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn,sliding-window",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290838",
          "text": "The input data is the string of $\\text{4 bits D = 1100}$. Assume the generator polynomial is defined by the following bit pattern $G = 1011$. Given $D$ and $G$ as above, find the $\\text{3 bits}$ for the CRC generated by the $\\text{CRC algorithm}$?<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $100$<br /> </li><li>  $101$<br /> </li> <li> $011$<br /> </li>  <li> $010$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290837",
          "text": "Suppose that in $\\text{RSA encryption}$, the public encryption key is the pair $(e, n)= (3, 55)$ and the private decryption key is the pair $(d,n)=55$, where $d$ is<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $13$<br /> </li><li>  $27$<br /> </li> <li> $37$<br /> </li>  <li> $39$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290836",
          "text": "The transport layer protocols used for SNMP, file transfer, email and DNS, respectively are:<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $\\text{TCP, UDP, UDP and TCP}$<br /> </li><li>  $\\text{UDP, TCP, TCP and UDP}$<br /> </li> <li> $\\text{UDP, TCP, UDP and TCP}$<br /> </li>  <li> $\\text{TCP, UDP, TCP and UDP}$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290835",
          "text": "Which of the following statements is false about $\\text{link state routing (LS)}$, and $\\text{distance vector routing (DV)}$<br />\n$S1:$ LS, DV both requires each router to obtain a map of the complete topology<br />\n$S2:$ DV requires ﬂooding<br />\n$S3:$ DV suﬀers from the count to inﬁnity problem<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  Only $S1$<br /> </li><li>  Only $S1$ and $S3$<br /> </li> <li> $S1$ and $S2$<br /> </li>  <li> Only $S2$ and $S3$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290834",
          "text": "<p>Consider an instance of TCP’s $\\text{Additive Increase Multiplicative Decrease (AIMD)}$ algorithm where the window size at the start of the slow start phase is $\\text{1 MSS}$ and the threshold at the start of the first transmission is $\\text{8 MSS}$. Assume that a timeout occurs during the sixth transmission and tenth transmission then what would be the window size at the $15^{th} \\hspace{0.1cm} transmission&nbsp;$?<br>\n&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$\\text{10 MSS}$</li>\n    <li>$\\text{6 MSS}$</li>\n    <li>$\\text{5 MSS}$</li>\n    <li>$\\text{7 MSS}$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn,congestion-control",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290833",
          "text": "Let the size of congestion window of a TCP connection be $\\text{64 KB}$ when a timeout occurs. The maximum segment size used is $\\text{4 KB}$. The time taken by the TCP connection to get back to $\\text{64 KB}$ congestion window is $\\text{7.2 sec}$. The round trip time in milliseconds is ________",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "654 : 655",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn,numerical-answers",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290832",
          "text": "Consider sending a $\\text{3000 byte}$ datagram into a link that has an $MTU$ of $\\text{500 bytes}$. Size of IP header is $\\text{20 bytes}$. Number of fragments generated is  ____",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "7",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn,ip-packet,numerical-answers",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290831",
          "text": "<p>Using the $CRC$ method, the remainder obtained by dividing $x^9 + x^7 + x^3 + x^1$ &nbsp; by generator polynomial $x^3 + x + 1$ ?&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$1$</li>\n    <li>$x$</li>\n    <li>$x^2$</li>\n    <li>$1+x + x^2$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290830",
          "text": "In a $\\text{RSA cryptosystem}$, a participant uses two prime numbers $7$ and $11$  to generate public and private keys. If the public key is $13$, then the private key is ____ <br />\n<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li> $32$<br /> </li><li> $33$<br /> </li> <li>$34$<br /> </li>  <li>$37$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290829",
          "text": "Determine the maximum length of the cable $\\text{(in km)}$ for transmitting data at a rate of $\\text{1 Gbps}$ in an $\\text{Ethernet LAN}$ with frames of size $\\text{4000 bits}$. Assume the signal speed in the cable to be $\\text{2,00,000 km/s}$.<br />\n<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li> $\\text{100 meters}$<br /> </li><li> $\\text{200 meters}$<br /> </li> <li>$\\text{400 meters}$<br /> </li>  <li>$\\text{500 meters}$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "290828",
          "text": "A network advertises the $CIDR$ network number $50.1.56.0/22$ (and no other  numbers).  Which of the following $\\text{IP addresses}$ could the network own? <br />\n<br />\n    1. $ 50.1.57.0 $<br />\n    2. $ 50.1.59.1 $<br />\n    3. $ 50.1.60.0 $<br />\n    4. $ 50.1.120.0 $<br />\n<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li> $\\text{Only 1}$<br /> </li><li> $\\text{Only 1 and 2}$<br /> </li> <li>$\\text{Only 1,2 and 3}$<br /> </li>  <li>$\\text{All of 1,2,3 and 4 }$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-gt-cn",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}